      <title>Nouveau: Cooking an open source driver</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>X.org</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Cooking a graphics driver involves a complex recipe and a number of ingredients. This talk will detail the recipe used for &lt;a href=&#34;http://nouveau.freedesktop.org/wiki/&#34;&gt;Nouveau&lt;/a&gt;, an open source 2D/3D nVidia driver.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We will focus on the required steps to get a nice meal, including 2D acceleration with EXA, 3D acceleration support using gallium, proper modesetting with dual head, improved Xv support, and what all this entails.&#xA;Less technical aspects like building a community around a driver will also be discussed.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We will finish by discussing future cooking, including moving more of the driver components into the kernel and possible extensions like fb support.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
